  <!-- SECTION 2: HETEROTIC GROUPS & ARCHITECTURE -->
  <section id="caas-groups" aria-labelledby="caas-groups-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="caas-groups-title">Heterotic groups</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="caas-groups-grid">
      <article class="caas-group-card">
        <h3>Tang Sipingtou \(TSPT\) &amp; Landrace Heritage</h3>
        <p>
          Derived from the foundational Chinese landrace selection Huangzaosi, the TSPT group \(Huangzaosi, Chang7-2, Jing92\) provides critical adaptation to northern cropping systems, exceptional combining ability, and stress tolerance when crossed with Stiff Stalk and P-Group lines.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="caas-group-card">
        <h3>P-Group Lineages \(PA &amp; PB\) &amp; Pioneer Heritage</h3>
        <p>
          Formed through the introgression of international Pioneer germplasm into Chinese breeding programs, P-Group A \(Ye478, Zheng58\) and P-Group B \(Xu178\) serve as foundational female parents for high-yielding commercial mega-hybrids such as Zhengdan 958.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="caas-group-card">
        <h3>Lancaster, Stiff Stalk &amp; Iodent Complementation</h3>
        <p>
          The integration of classical US Corn Belt heterotic groups—including Lancaster Surecrop \(Dan340, Oh43\), Stiff Stalk \(A632\), and Iodent \(PH207\)—provides broad genetic diversity and complementary alleles driving hybrid performance and grain yield.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3: KEY PUBLICATIONS & ABSTRACT PREVIEWS -->
  <section id="caas-publications" aria-labelledby="caas-pub-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="caas-pub-title">Publications</h2></div>
