      $(reference_cards)
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4: DATA HOSTED AT MAIZEGDB -->
  <section id="caas-data-hosted" aria-labelledby="caas-hosted-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="caas-hosted-title">Hosted data</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="caas-hosted-grid">
      <!-- 1: JBrowse 2 -->
      <article class="caas-hosted-card">
        <h3>Genome Browsers \(JBrowse 2\)</h3>
        <p>Interactive chromosome-scale browsers for all 12 CAAS founder lines with gene models, repeat elements, and comparative tracks.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/genomebrowser">Open Genome Browsers &#8599;</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 2: Gene Center -->
      <article class="caas-hosted-card">
        <h3>Gene Center &amp; Models</h3>
        <p>Over 530,000 high-confidence gene models across the 12 assemblies indexed in the Gene Center with functional annotations.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/gene_center/gene">Explore Gene Center &#8599;</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 3: BLAST -->
      <article class="caas-hosted-card">
        <h3>Sequence BLAST Tool</h3>
        <p>Align nucleotide, CDS, transcript, and translated protein queries directly against CAAS-FIL assemblies and gene models.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="$(blast_url)">Run BLAST Search &#8599;</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 4: Bulk Downloads -->
      <article class="caas-hosted-card">
        <h3>Bulk Downloads &amp; Globus</h3>
        <p>Download complete assembly FASTA files, GFF3 annotations, canonical CDS/PEP sequences, and pre-indexed tracks.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/download#downloads-caas-fil">Browse Downloads &#8599;</a>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: SCALE & GENOMIC METRICS DASHBOARD -->
  <section id="caas-faqs" aria-labelledby="caas-faqs-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="caas-faqs-title">FAQs</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="caas-faq-list">
      <details class="caas-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Why are founder inbred lines \(FILs\) critical for maize genetics?</h3></summary>
        <div class="caas-faq-body">
          <p>
            Founder inbred lines represent the foundational genetic pillars of modern hybrid breeding programs. Over 80% of modern Chinese commercial maize acreage traces to crosses between these founder lines \(for example, the mega-hybrid Zhengdan 958 derived from Zheng58 &times; Chang7-2\). Having high-quality reference genomes for all 12 founders illuminates the genetic combinations and structural alleles driving hybrid vigor.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="caas-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Where can I download FASTA sequences and GFF3 gene annotations?</h3></summary>
        <div class="caas-faq-body">
          <p>
            Full assembly FASTA files, GFF3 gene annotations, CDS/PEP files, and NCBI GenBank accessions are available on the <a href="/download#downloads-caas-fil">MaizeGDB Downloads Portal</a> or via individual assembly links in the table above.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="caas-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>How do CAAS-FIL gene models compare with B73 and Mo17?</h3></summary>
        <div class="caas-faq-body">
          <p>
            While B73 and Mo17 represent classical US Stiff Stalk and Lancaster references, the CAAS-FIL assemblies uncover extensive novel gene models, structural rearrangements, and presence-absence variants specific to the Tang Sipingtou and P-Group lineages. Comparative synteny tracks are viewable directly in <a href="/genomebrowser">JBrowse 2</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="caas-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Can I run BLAST against individual CAAS founder genomes?</h3></summary>
        <div class="caas-faq-body">
          <p>
            Yes! MaizeGDB hosts dedicated BLAST databases for all 12 CAAS lines. Navigate to the <a href="$(blast_url)">BLAST Tool</a> and select the desired CAAS assembly or predicted peptide database.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

  </section>

